Mitcad patch (mitcad#343): faces taken for tangent along an edge whose
curves on them lie apart by up to ten times its tolerance.

ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces compares the two faces along the edge with
LocalAnalysis_SurfaceContinuity, the points of the edge's curves on the two
faces within max(0.001, 1.5 x the edge's tolerance) of each other. Each of
those curves may lie within the tolerance of the edge's own curve, so the
two up to twice the tolerance apart; on the bodies stored in files the
approximated edges of a thread (helices of seven turns, tolerances of 1.4
to 3.7 micrometres) have curves on their faces up to 4.8 micrometres off
their own. A thread's crest rounded on both edges by an earlier rounding,
the crest band and the two roundings tangent to each other (within 1e-3
radian) and to the flanks: the edges between them failed the position test,
and so the faces were taken for faces meeting at an angle. A rounding round
the thread's chamfer cone then stopped its contour at the vertices of those
edges (FaceTangency) and was three roundings meeting end to end, which
walked past their common vertices over each other; and the walk of one
rounding across such an edge stopped there (IsG1 in SearchFace). The
positions are now compared within ten times the edge's tolerance (at least
0.001 as before; the normals within a tenth of a radian as before).

